    "q-148433": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148433",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{6}{5x+3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5x+3}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{6}{5y+3}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{6}{5y+3} \\\\ x(5y+3) & =6 \\\\ 5xy+3x & =6 \\\\ 5xy & =6-3x \\\\ y & =\\frac{6-3x}{5x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6-3x}{5x}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
